# Git Flow

## Branch

After a tracker ticket exists, create and check out a branch **before** writing code:

```bash
git checkout -b feature/<TICKET-KEY>
```

- Exact key from the tracker (`PROJ-123`). Do not invent keys.
- Allowed prefixes: `feature/`, `bugfix/`, `hotfix/`.
- **No slug after the number** — `feature/PROJ-123` only, never `feature/PROJ-123-short-name`.
- Do not work on `main` / `master` / `dev` / `test` / `stage` / `demo` / `prod` for ticket work.
- Confirm with `git branch --show-current` that the ticket branch is checked out before editing files.

## Commit

Format (enforced by `.githooks/commit-msg`):

```text
feature/PROJ-123 - Short description
```

Types: `feature`, `bugfix`, `hotfix`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `style`, `release`.

- Commit only when the human asks.
- Never pass `--no-verify`.
- Prefer HEREDOC for the message body.

## Merge requests

Target the integration branch (`dev` unless the repo says otherwise). Open ready for review unless the human asks for draft.
